        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Elective monarchy</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">633 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Power held by</span><span class="info-stat-val">The elected monarch, usually for life, often bound by conditions the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> imposed as the price of the crown, such as electoral capitulations or the Polish pacta conventa</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Legitimacy from</span><span class="info-stat-val">Choice by a recognised body of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a>, usually from a royal house or a qualified class, sealed by oath, coronation or religious consecration</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How rulers are chosen</span><span class="info-stat-val">Elected on the ruler’s death or abdication, sometimes in his lifetime, by prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a>, the assembled nobility, a council of rulers or cardinals; in Malaysia for a five-year term</span></div>
